# PROJECT: AFRICAN CROWNS — EMPIRES OF THE SUN

## YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior mobile game developer, real-time strategy game designer, gameplay programmer, UI/UX designer, historical research consultant, and software architect.

Your task is to build a genuinely playable, visually impressive, historically inspired African kingdom-building and real-time strategy game called:

AFRICAN CROWNS: EMPIRES OF THE SUN

The game takes inspiration from the settlement construction, economic management, fortification building, military strategy, siege gameplay, and campaign structure of classic castle-building strategy games such as Stronghold Crusader.

However, this must be an original game with its own identity, mechanics, architecture, art direction, civilizations, progression systems, and historical setting.

Do not copy proprietary assets, maps, characters, sounds, interfaces, or other protected content from existing games.

The game must celebrate the diversity, engineering, trade, political organization, architecture, craftsmanship, agriculture, and cultural achievements of African civilizations.

This is a serious game-development project, not a static prototype or a collection of attractive menus.

The primary goal is to deliver a playable Android-friendly game with functioning construction, resource management, population simulation, economic systems, AI-controlled rivals, and real-time battles.

Build a small but complete game first. Expand it through carefully tested iterations.

---

# 1. PLATFORM AND TECHNICAL DIRECTION

Build this project as a mobile-first, installable Progressive Web App (PWA) using Google AI Studio's full-stack web application mode.

The target devices are Android smartphones.

The game must run in a mobile browser, support installation on the Android home screen where supported, and provide an app-like experience.

Use the following technical direction:

- Frontend: React and TypeScript.
- Game rendering: HTML5 Canvas or another lightweight 2D rendering solution appropriate for real-time strategy games.
- Backend: Node.js when required for online functionality.
- Multiplayer infrastructure: a suitable authoritative server architecture, with Firebase services where appropriate.
- Persistence: local save support for single-player games, plus server-side persistence for online accounts and multiplayer sessions.
- Graphics: original procedural artwork, original SVG assets, CSS illustrations, and generated game assets that can legally be used in the project.
- Audio: original or properly licensed audio, with a functional mute and volume system.

Choose stable, compatible libraries only when they materially improve the game.

Avoid unnecessary dependencies and heavyweight 3D engines.

Do not require a dedicated GPU.

Do not make the game depend on a Gemini API call for every movement, battle, resource calculation, or building action. Ordinary gameplay must run through deterministic game logic.

The game should remain playable if optional AI-generated dialogue or other remote AI features are unavailable.

Do not expose secret keys in client-side code.

IMPORTANT: Online multiplayer requires a real backend and server-authoritative game state. Do not simulate multiplayer by displaying fake players or pretending that local computer-controlled opponents are connected users.

