# 19. PERFORMANCE REQUIREMENTS

The primary target is a reasonably modern Android smartphone, including mid-range devices.

The game must prioritize stable performance and battery efficiency.

Requirements:

- Use lightweight 2D graphics.
- Avoid unnecessary rendering work.
- Avoid excessive numbers of animated entities.
- Keep pathfinding and simulation costs under control.
- Avoid full-screen React rerenders for every individual game tick.
- Separate the rendering loop from the interface state where appropriate.
- Pause or reduce simulation when the game is not visible, where appropriate.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences for interface animations.
- Handle browser resizing and returning from background states safely.
- Avoid memory leaks and runaway timers.
- Keep the interface readable at narrow screen widths.

Aim for smooth gameplay, targeting approximately 30–60 frames per second on suitable devices.

Treat this as a performance goal, not a guarantee.

When necessary, reduce animation density before reducing the clarity of the gameplay interface.

